Package: mlr3autoiml
Type: Package
Title: Claim-Scoped Diagnostic Gates for Interpretable Machine Learning
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Stefan", "Coors", email = "mail@stefancoors.de", role = c("aut","cre")),
    person("Clara", "Vetter", role = "aut"),
    person("Jonas", "Hauck", role = "aut"),
    person("Bernd", "Bischl", role = "aut"),
    person("Sven", "Hilbert", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Implements Claim-Scoped Diagnostic Gates (CSDG), a framework for
    deciding whether evidence supports a conclusion drawn from an explanation
    of a machine learning model. Users write the claim, specify its scope
    (quantity, model, procedure, data, meaning, and use), derive the
    properties it requires from a catalog of 12 gates, evaluate each property
    as supported, contradicted, or open, and apply a fixed decision rule under
    which a claim is met, not met, or unresolved. The package integrates with
    the 'mlr3' ecosystem and computes diagnostics such as held-out permutation
    feature importance, corrected resampled intervals, calibration,
    cross-fitted local fidelity of local surrogates, stability, and
    comparisons across models, settings, and subgroups. An analysis-first
    interface fits learners on common splits, computes held-out permutation
    feature importance, derives claims from the results, and computes the
    standard checks and the assessment. Favorable evidence
    never offsets a contradicted property, and no aggregate score is
    computed. The earlier 'AutoIML' workflow remains available for
    compatibility.
